" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKA SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORII KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORII, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A clutch, comprising drivingly rotating bodies (11; 52; 83; 202; 302) connected to a drive source (2) such as a motor and drivenly rotating bodies (12; 53; 85; 204; 303) engaged directly with the drivingly rotating bodies, wherein both rotating bodies are stored in housings (13; 51; 82; 201; 301), lock members (14; 54; 86; 119; 205; 304) comprising rollers and balls are disposed between the drivenly rotating bodies and the housings, when the drivenly rotating bodies themselves are rotated, the lock members are held between the drivenly rotating bodies and housings so that a rotation of the drivenly rotating bodies relative to the housings is prevented, when the drive source rotates the drivingly rotating bodies, the lock members reset the holding condition so as to allow the drivingly rotating bodies to rotate the drivenly rotating bodies relative to the housings, whereby the clutch can prevent securely a transmission of rotation from the drivenly rotating bodies to the drivingly rotating bodies and, in addition, strengths required for both rotating bodies can be reduced.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On décrit un embrayage comprenant des pièces rotatives menantes (11; 52; 83; 202; 302) connectées à une source d'excitation (2), telle qu'un moteur, et des pièces rotatives menées (12; 53; 85; 204; 303) en contact direct avec les pièces rotatives menantes. Chacun des deux types de pièces rotatives est logé dans un boîtier (13; 51; 82; 201; 304) et des éléments de verrouillage (14; 54; 86; 119; 205; 304) munis de galets et de billes sont disposés entre les pièces rotatives menées et les boîtiers. Lorsque les pièces rotatives menées sont en rotation, les éléments de verrouillage sont retenus entre les pièces rotatives menées et les boîtiers, ce qui empêche une rotation des pièces rotatives menées relativement aux boîtiers. Lorsque la source d'excitation impulse les pièces rotatives menantes, les éléments de verrouillage se remettent à l'état initial de retenue pour amener les pièces rotatives menantes à faire tourner les pièces rotatives menées relativement aux boîtiers, si bien que l'embrayage empêche de manière sûre une transmission de rotation des pièces rotatives menées aux pièces rotatives menantes, ce qui permet en outre de réduire la puissance requise pour entraîner les deux types de pièces.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>